From ff92a737f702c5c8ccfe0fb6494b2c2b2af91cb2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 17:09:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] A fourth source: USGS daily values, where the quantity is a
 statistic

The `daily` collection of the USGS Water Data OGC API, as an adapter, a
per-value extractor, a binding, 15 tests and docs/PHASE_45_USGS_DAILY_VALUES.md.

The endpoint was read before the module was written, not after: items come back
in no time order, `value` is a string, `time` is a bare date with no zone
anywhere in the response, paging is by opaque cursor, and nothing states a
per-value uncertainty.

Two refusals are the point of the phase.

A paged window is refused, not stitched. A RawDocument is one HTTP response
byte for byte in every adapter here; stitching pages would fabricate bytes no
server sent, and one document per page would make identity depend on `limit`
and on server-side cursor state. Instead the window is bounded (366 days
against a page limit of 10000) so a daily series is always one response, and
fetch() raises if a `next` link ever appears. It does not quietly return the
first page: a silent truncation is a lost day of water that nothing downstream
could detect.

And the date keeps its silence. Writing 2023-01-07 as a local-standard-time
instant, or calling it a UTC day, would have been one line. Legacy NWIS practice
says the former; this API does not. measurement_time is the bare date, verbatim,
and what a day means is a declaration for whoever consumes it -- the same
discipline Phase 32 applied to uncertainty, applied to time.

`method` carries the verbatim statistic_id, per Phase 31. It is load-bearing
here rather than decorative: a daily mean, maximum and minimum of one parameter
at one site on one day are three quantities that are otherwise identical in
content.

The binding takes no scientific parameters at all. NOAA's must carry datum and
units to both halves because its response echoes neither; USGS states every
dimension in each item, so the extractor reads what the adapter requested and
there is nothing that can drift.

Three of this repository's own checks refused the first draft, and all three
were right:

- test_no_extractor_declares_a_conditions_key. The draft built a conditions
  FrozenMapping of parameter_code and statistic_id. The values came from the
  response, but the decision that those two fields ARE the conditions came from
  the extractor, and section 20 forbids exactly that. Removed: the source states
  no measurement conditions, so none are recorded, and `method` already
  distinguishes the statistics.
- test_an_anchor_has_landed_and_this_guard_is_retired. The new fixture is now
  declared, so an undeclared one still fails.
- test_bitemporality_is_recorded_as_half_present_and_still_is. Valid time now
  sits in two extractors' content rather than one. The recorded position is
  updated to say so, because two extractors each inventing a content key for
  valid time is what "not a platform dimension" looks like; the list stays exact
  so a third is noticed.

Suite: 2553 passed, with only the six failures this checkout already had before
this branch (they need full git history, which a shallow clone does not have).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
